│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sphere_softmin_optimization                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The random configuration gives essentially zero ratio. A good structure for this problem  │
│                          │ is points on a sphere (which fixes dmax near the diameter for antipodal-ish spreads, and  │
│                          │ normalizing lets the ratio equal dmin/dmax of the unit-sphere configuration). I optimize  │
│                          │ a Tammes-like problem: place 14 points on the unit sphere maximizing the minimum pairwise │
│                          │ distance, using a smooth soft-min surrogate (logsumexp with decreasing temperature)       │
│                          │ minimized with L-BFGS-B, from several fixed-seed restarts. The configuration with the     │
│                          │ best actual dmin/dmax ratio is returned. This is the known best approach for such         │
│                          │ "max-min / min-max" point-spreading problems and should reach a squared ratio near the    │
│                          │ reference ~1/4.166 (ratio ≈ 0.49, achieved by the optimal 14-point spherical arrangement  │
│                          │ with several antipodal pairs).                                                            │
