│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stronger_multistart_optimization                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The reference squared ratio is 1/4.1658 ≈ 0.24003. The current program achieves ~0.22     │
│                          │ (ratio ~0.47). A key issue is the soft-min/soft-max surrogate at fixed temperatures gets  │
│                          │ stuck, and the objective is scale-invariant, so the optimizer wastes effort on scale.     │
│                          │ Improvements: (1) renormalize points (centroid to origin, dmax=1) after each optimization │
│                          │ stage so the optimizer focuses purely on shape; (2) use more restarts with a dedicated    │
│                          │ seeded RNG and slightly larger perturbations for diversity; (3) add a final direct        │
│                          │ hill-climbing polish that perturbs each point greedily, accepting only moves that         │
│                          │ increase the true ratio dmin/dmax — this directly targets the actual metric; (4) also try │
│                          │ a second initialization from a randomized arrangement (points on a sphere with jittered   │
│                          │ angles) for a different basin. These are cheap and fit comfortably within the timeout.    │
