│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign: instead of returning raw random points, the program is organized     │
│                          │ into small pipeline stages — (1) a seeded multi-restart generator producing candidate     │
│                          │ initial point sets, (2) a force-directed refinement loop on the unit sphere that pushes   │
│                          │ apart close pairs using a soft-min gradient, and (3) a selection stage that scores each   │
│                          │ candidate config directly with the evaluator's metric (dmin/dmax)² and keeps the best.    │
│                          │ This modular data flow (generate → refine → score → select) robustly finds a near-optimal │
│                          │ spherical arrangement of 14 points, dramatically raising the min/max distance ratio while │
│                          │ remaining fast and reproducible via fixed seeds.                                          │
