│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tammes14_structured_inits_and_polish                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ For n=14 in 3D, the optimal ratio (≈0.49, matching the reference squared ratio ≈0.2398)   │
│                          │ is essentially attained by Tammes-type spherical arrangements — packings of 14 points on  │
│                          │ a sphere that avoid antipodal pairs so the diameter is only slightly above 2 while the    │
│                          │ minimal chord approaches ~1.03. The current optimizer gets 0.22 (ratio≈0.47), so there is │
│                          │ a real gap caused by poor local optima. Two targeted improvements:                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Add high-quality structured initializations that mimic the known Tammes-14 families:   │
│                          │ two staggered hexagonal rings plus two poles (D6-like symmetry), and an icosahedron shell │
│                          │ with two symmetric mid-latitude points. These start the optimizer very close to the       │
│                          │ global optimum.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Replace the single final polish with an iterated "perturb-and-polish" scheme:          │
│                          │ repeatedly perturb the current best with decreasing magnitude and re-polish with the      │
│                          │ softmin/softmax gradient, accepting improvements. This escapes shallow local optima       │
│                          │ deterministically (fixed seed) and monotonically improves the best candidate, all within  │
│                          │ a modest time budget.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
