│ patch_description        │ The best-known ratio-optimal 14-point arrangement in 3D has D6 symmetry: two staggered    │
│                          │ hexagonal rings (radius r, heights ±h, relative twist π/6) plus two poles (0,0,±p). For   │
│                          │ this configuration all pairwise distances have closed forms, so I first run an exact      │
│                          │ dense grid/local search over the three parameters (p, h, r) maximizing dmin/dmax          │
│                          │ directly. This gives a seed essentially at the true optimum (squared ratio target         │
│                          │ 1/4.165849767 ≈ 0.2400). I then run the existing soft-min/soft-max projected gradient     │
│                          │ polish on this seed (and a few jittered variants, plus the icosahedron fallback) to       │
│                          │ squeeze out any residual improvement, keeping the best configuration found. This replaces │
│                          │ the previously geometrically-mismatched starting points, letting the local optimizer      │
│                          │ polish straight to the symmetric optimum instead of trying to discover it.                │
