│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ d6_symmetric_seed_polish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of hoping a local optimizer discovers the right geometry from generic seeds, I    │
│                          │ directly construct the known D6-symmetric Tammes-14 candidate family (two staggered       │
│                          │ hexagonal rings at z=±h plus two poles at z=±z0), which is the conjectured optimum        │
│                          │ matching the reference squared ratio 1/4.165849767 ≈ 0.24005. The family has only two     │
│                          │ effective degrees of freedom (scale-invariant), so I grid-search and Nelder-Mead-refine   │
│                          │ (R, h, z0) to maximize the exact ratio. Then I polish with the annealed soft-min/soft-max │
│                          │ L-BFGS-B schedule from the prior programs — starting exactly at the symmetric optimum, so │
│                          │ the polish only needs to confirm/round it rather than discover it. A few jittered         │
│                          │ restarts guard against numerical slop, and the best result by true ratio is returned.     │
│                          │ This is fast (no large multi-seed SLSQP runs) and lands precisely on the symmetric        │
│                          │ optimum.                                                                                  │
