│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_tammes_slsqp                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Fundamentally different from the current annealing-only approach: a two-stage hybrid.     │
│                          │ Stage 1 is a fast force-directed relaxation on the unit sphere (multi-restart, adaptive   │
│                          │ repulsion cutoff) that reliably reaches good Tammes-like configurations (~0.86 score      │
│                          │ proven in an earlier generation). Stage 2 — new — converts the best spherical             │
│                          │ configurations into a direct maximin optimization solved with SLSQP: maximize the         │
│                          │ variable t subject to dmin² ≥ t² and dmax² ≤ 1, which directly optimizes the exact        │
│                          │ evaluator metric (dmin/dmax)², not just a proxy. This lifts the pure sphere constraint,   │
│                          │ letting SLSQP fine-tune point positions freely in R³ to squeeze out extra ratio. Wrapped  │
│                          │ in try/except with a valid fallback so it always returns a finite (14,3) array.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
