│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pair_triple_hillclimb_polish                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Add a targeted greedy hill-climb stage that directly manipulates the distance pairs that  │
│                          │ matter: the pair realizing the current minimum distance (push them apart along their      │
│                          │ separation direction) and the pair realizing the maximum distance (pull them toward each  │
│                          │ other), plus a coordinated triple move doing both simultaneously. Single-coordinate or    │
│                          │ smooth-gradient polishes often stall on plateaus because improving the ratio requires     │
│                          │ coordinated displacement of both endpoints. This stage uses exact ratio evaluation with   │
│                          │ an accept/reject shrinking step, is scale-invariant (re-normalizes diameter to 1), and is │
│                          │ cheap (91 pairs). It is appended after Stage 5 so it can only improve the result.         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
