│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ softmin_annealing_with_clipped_exponentials                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a gradient-based annealing stage that maximizes a smooth soft-min/soft-max surrogate  │
│                          │ of the ratio using exponentially-weighted distance aggregation. A soft-min (log-sum-exp   │
│                          │ of -d/tau) and soft-max (log-sum-exp of +d/tau) give differentiable lower/upper bounds on │
│                          │ dmin/dmax, so gradient ascent on their ratio smoothly approaches the true discrete metric │
│                          │ as tau shrinks. A tau schedule annealing down to 0.002 and 0.001 (with exp arguments      │
│                          │ clipped to ±50 for numerical safety) sharpens the surrogate before the existing           │
│                          │ force-relax and SLSQP polish, letting the hill-climb start from a better basin. This      │
│                          │ directly implements the recommendation of extending the annealing floor below 0.005 with  │
│                          │ clipped exponentials, and it complements (rather than replaces) the existing discrete     │
│                          │ stages.                                                                                   │
