│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_greedy_climb_and_d6_grid_seeds                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program relies on annealed soft-min L-BFGS-B from a single Tammes-like seed   │
│                          │ plus random starts, reaching ratio ~0.22. The prior best program (score 0.93) showed that │
│                          │ the D6 family (two staggered hexagonal rings plus two poles) with a fine grid search over │
│                          │ (h, z0), plus an exact greedy hill-climb on the true dmin/dmax ratio, reliably squeezes   │
│                          │ out extra ratio. I therefore (1) add a parametric grid search over the D6 family to seed  │
│                          │ the optimizer with the exact symmetric near-optimum, and (2) append a greedy coordinated  │
│                          │ pair-move hill-climb on the true ratio after the L-BFGS-B annealing, which can make       │
│                          │ strict improvements that smooth objectives miss. Both stages are cheap and keep runtime   │
│                          │ well under the timeout.                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0160                                                                                   │
