├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ d6_parametric_scan_direct                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Prior generations repeatedly converge "near" the D6-symmetric                             │
│                          │ two-hexagonal-rings-plus-poles basin but the generic force-directed relaxation is too     │
│                          │ noisy to land exactly on the symmetric optimum. Instead of only adding the D6 rings as    │
│                          │ force-relaxation seeds, we should exploit the family's low-dimensional parametrization    │
│                          │ directly: sweep the ring height h and stagger twist finely on a grid, score each          │
│                          │ configuration exactly with the true objective, and then feed only the top few exact       │
│                          │ configurations into the free-space SLSQP maximin polish. Because the D6 family has only   │
│                          │ 2-3 effective parameters (h, twist, and implicitly the unit-sphere radius constraint), a  │
│                          │ dense grid scan plus polish essentially solves the symmetric subproblem exactly,          │
│                          │ guaranteeing the pipeline starts and ends inside the best-known basin rather than near    │
│                          │ it. We add a `_d6_direct_scan` helper that returns the best few (h, twist) configurations │
│                          │ polished by SLSQP, and inject them as already-relaxed candidates at the top of the        │
│                          │ candidate list, so they compete directly with (and typically beat) the relaxed random     │
│                          │ starts. This costs little time (a few dozen cheap evaluations plus a couple of SLSQP      │
│                          │ calls) and directly targets the 0.21-0.22 ratio plateau where the best-known structures   │
│                          │ live.                                                                                     │
