│ patch_name               │ add_repulsion_and_random_seeds                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program is confined to the D6-symmetric basin: every candidate passed to      │
│                          │ `polish` is either the exact D6 parametric optimum or a tiny jitter of it, so the         │
│                          │ soft-min/soft-max annealing can never discover asymmetric configurations that may beat    │
│                          │ the D6 family (the reference squared ratio 1/4.1658 corresponds to ratio ≈ 0.49, and the  │
│                          │ earlier general-seed program reached 0.24 squared ratio vs. 0.22 here). Two targeted      │
│                          │ changes: (1) add a short force-based repulsion relaxation (each point is pushed away from │
│                          │ its nearest neighbor, followed by re-normalization) applied before the L-BFGS-B annealing │
│                          │ — this spreads cramped seeds apart so the annealed soft objective starts from a           │
│                          │ well-conditioned configuration; (2) diversify Stage 4 by adding, besides the jittered D6  │
│                          │ restarts, several random-on-sphere seeds and small D6-perturbation seeds with larger      │
│                          │ magnitude, each pre-conditioned by repulsion and then fully annealed/polished. All        │
│                          │ candidates still go through the existing hill-climb stages, so quality can only improve.  │
│                          │ The repulsion is cheap (vectorized, ~100 iterations) so the runtime stays well within     │
│                          │ timeout.                                                                                  │
