│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_pair_move_hillclimb                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation is exactly right: single-coordinate moves cannot fix the ratio because │
│                          │ improving it usually requires moving the two closest points apart along their separating  │
│                          │ direction (both must move) and pulling the two farthest points inward. I add a dedicated  │
│                          │ `_pair_hillclimb` polisher that, at each step, identifies the pair realizing dmin and     │
│                          │ pushes both points apart along their connecting direction, and identifies the pair        │
│                          │ realizing dmax and pulls both inward, trying several step sizes and greedily accepting    │
│                          │ any move that improves (dmin/dmax)^2. It repeats until no improvement. This is cheap (14  │
│                          │ points, O(1) pairs per step) and directly targets the only two distances that matter to   │
│                          │ the objective. It is inserted after the SLSQP polish and inside the perturbation loop.    │
