│                          │ the two perturbation loops around the incumbent (perturbations of 0.02–0.13 and           │
│                          │ 0.004–0.019). The main opportunity per the analysis is a stronger mid-scale               │
│                          │ perturb-and-reanneal loop around the *incumbent best* — larger kicks (~0.05–0.15) with a  │
│                          │ full annealing ladder, which explores nearby basins more aggressively than the current    │
│                          │ small-kick polish loop. I add a dedicated 8-trial reanneal loop with growing perturbation │
│                          │ scales (0.05 + 0.012*trial) and a slightly longer tau ladder, plus keep the               │
│                          │ low-temperature polish. To stay within the timeout, the seed sweep uses a shorter ladder  │
│                          │ and fewer maxfun. Expected gain: better escape from local basins around the D6-type       │
│                          │ optimum, pushing the ratio above 0.24.                                                    │
