│ patch_description        │ The best prior program (score 0.99, ratio 0.24) started from an icosahedron + 2 polar     │
│                          │ points and used an annealed soft objective followed by greedy coordinate descent. The     │
│                          │ current program's D6 double-ring family gets stuck at ratio 0.22 (score 0.92). I          │
│                          │ therefore replace the main construction with: (1) an icosahedron-plus-poles               │
│                          │ initialization (also compared against the D6 parametric optimum so we never regress), (2) │
│                          │ the existing annealed soft-min/soft-max `polish`, and (3) a greedy coordinate descent on  │
│                          │ the exact ratio with adaptive per-point step sizes as recommended: binding points (those  │
│                          │ in the min-distance and max-distance pairs) get larger steps (0.05–0.1) while non-binding │
│                          │ points get small steps (0.01), concentrating the 14×3×2 sweep budget on coordinates that  │
│                          │ actually affect the binding constraints. This preserves the exact-ratio convergence of    │
│                          │ the greedy stage while cutting wasted evaluations and improving the achievable ratio.     │
