│                          │ rather than only perturbing at trial initialization, re-perturb the best solution found   │
│                          │ so far and run full annealing chains again. I combine this with structured seeds from the │
│                          │ context programs (the staggered double-hexagon D6 family with poles, the icosahedron+2    │
│                          │ construction, and random sphere points), all funneled through a shared annealed           │
│                          │ soft-min/soft-max polish that works directly on d² (scale-invariant up to normalization). │
│                          │ After the seeded trials, 10 perturb-reanneal restarts at 0.08 noise around the incumbent  │
│                          │ explore the basin around the best configuration — this is where prior gains               │
│                          │ plateau-breaking occurred. A final greedy targeted pair-move hill-climb squeezes out      │
