│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the prior annealed soft-min/soft-max programs, this version makes a cleaner,  │
│                          │ faster pipeline: (1) a compact seed library (D6 double rings + poles, icosahedron+poles,  │
│                          │ twisted heptagons, random spheres), (2) an annealed L-BFGS-B ladder over a clipped        │
│                          │ soft-min/soft-max ratio with tau driven down to 0.001 using np.clip(±dv/tau, -50, 50) for │
│                          │ numerical safety, (3) a deterministic hard-ratio polish that directly maximizes the true  │
│                          │ discrete ratio via iterative exact line search along min-pair/max-pair directions (no     │
│                          │ soft surrogate gap remains), and (4) perturb-reanneal restarts with a fixed seed. The key │
│                          │ insight is that the clipped anneal gets close to the true optimum basin, and the hard     │
│                          │ polish — which needs no tau and thus has no surrogate gap — closes the remaining          │
│                          │ distance, matching the reference squared ratio of 1/4.1658 while running in well under    │
│                          │ the timeout.                                                                              │
