│ patch_name               │ epigraph_slsqp_tammes14                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Fundamentally different approach: instead of soft-min gradient ascent, formulate the      │
│                          │ problem as an exact epigraph (minimax) nonlinear program — maximize t subject to t² ≤     │
│                          │ ||xi−xj||² for all pairs and ||xi−xj||² ≤ 1 (diameter capped at 1) — and solve it with    │
│                          │ SLSQP from many structured inits (twisted heptagon bi-rings, staggered hexagonal rings    │
│                          │ with poles, icosahedron + axis pair, random). Since the ratio is scale-invariant, capping │
│                          │ dmax at 1 makes t exactly the min/max ratio. Soft-min ascent on the sphere is used only   │
│                          │ as a cheap pre-conditioner to feed good starting points into the exact constrained        │
│                          │ solver, then the exact solution is polished with perturb-and-reoptimize rounds on the     │
│                          │ true nonsmooth objective. This directly maximizes the true ratio instead of a smoothed    │
│                          │ surrogate, which is where the previous gradient approach plateaued at 0.21.               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
