│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_soft_ratio_polish_stage                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program relies only on a repulsion-style relaxation, which converges to       │
│                          │ configurations where the min distance is "locally pushed" but is not a true local optimum │
│                          │ of the ratio dmin/dmax. A complementary, well-proven technique (used in the               │
│                          │ higher-scoring variants) is an annealed smooth surrogate: replace dmin and dmax by        │
│                          │ soft-min/soft-max over squared distances via logsumexp, and minimize that surrogate with  │
│                          │ L-BFGS while annealing tau to zero. This gradient-based method makes coordinated,         │
│                          │ simultaneous moves of all 14 points (unlike the greedy pairwise repulsion), and since the │
│                          │ objective is built from squared distances it is smooth and well-conditioned for the       │
│                          │ optimizer. Adding this as a final polish stage applied to the best relaxed configuration, │
│                          │ plus a few jittered polish restarts, should refine the ratio beyond what relaxation alone │
│                          │ reaches, matching or beating the ~0.94 score of the best prior program while staying well │
│                          │ within the time budget (the polish takes ~1s). The polish re-centers and re-normalizes    │
│                          │ (scale-invariant surrogate on d^2), so the returned points remain valid and normalized to │
│                          │ unit diameter.                                                                            │
