│ patch_description        │ Keeps the proven machinery (soft-min/soft-max annealed L-BFGS polish plus exact greedy    │
│                          │ hill-climb) but restructures the compute budget per the recommendation: Phase 1 is        │
│                          │ trimmed to a compact seed library (D6 ring grid, Tammes seed, a twisted-heptagon          │
│                          │ antiprism family, and two random seeds) instead of an expensive sweep, and the saved time │
│                          │ is reinvested in many perturb-and-reanneal restarts around the incumbent. The anneal      │
│                          │ chain uses a scale-invariant free-space objective (soft-min of distances plus soft-max)   │
│                          │ so both the numerator and denominator of the ratio are optimized jointly, and each        │
│                          │ annealed candidate is hill-climbed on the exact ratio for fine polish. Everything is      │
│                          │ deterministic (fixed seeds) and normalized to unit diameter before return.                │
