│ patch_name               │ add_scipy_polish_and_pair_climb                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program only uses a repulsion relaxation, which plateaus at ratio^2 ≈ 0.22    │
│                          │ (score 0.93). Prior generations showed that adding (a) an annealed soft-min/soft-max      │
│                          │ L-BFGS polish and (b) a vectorized steepest-ascent hill climb that moves all binding      │
│                          │ min/max pairs simultaneously (the "multi-pair binding-constraint" strategy from the       │
│                          │ recommendations) pushes the score to ~0.94+. I add both as post-processing stages: every  │
│                          │ relax result gets a short polish + climb, and the final winner gets a high-precision      │
│                          │ polish and a multi-pair climb. This is targeted: the relax stage stays as the global      │
│                          │ basin search, while the new stages do the fine convergence on the true objective. To stay │
│                          │ within timeout, climb uses multi-pair candidate generation (all pairs within 5% of        │
│                          │ dmin/dmax) and polish uses a small tau ladder.                                            │
