│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tangential_pair_polish                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current pair_polish only tries pure axial separation of the closest pair and axial    │
│                          │ contraction of the diameter pair. When a third neighbor sits along the pair axis, axial   │
│                          │ moves can be blocked, and the polish stalls. Following the recommendation, I add          │
│                          │ tangential candidate moves: when separating the closest pair, both points are also        │
│                          │ displaced with a tangential component perpendicular to the pair direction (and to the     │
│                          │ local z-axis of the pair, giving a well-defined tangent plane), at 0.3·step magnitude.    │
│                          │ This generates extra candidates per step size that let the pair "slide around" nearby     │
│                          │ obstacles at the same step scale, which can push the exact ratio past what axial moves    │
│                          │ achieve. I also apply a symmetric tangential variant for contracting the diameter pair.   │
│                          │ All candidates are accepted only on strict exact-ratio improvement, so the procedure can  │
│                          │ never degrade the result. This is a cheap change to the existing polish loop and should   │
│                          │ not increase runtime materially since it replaces unused improvement potential within the │
│                          │ same rounds budget.                                                                       │
